---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const meta = [
  ['Role', 'Design + front-end'],
  ['Year', '2021, rerun 2022'],
  ['Stack', 'React, Firebase'],
  ['Scale', '40+ employers'],
];
const stats = [
  ['100+', 'Interviews scheduled'],
  ['3', 'Screens, student flow'],
  ['2', 'Years in service'],
];
---
<Base
  title="Virtual Career Fair Platform"
  description="A scheduling app built in six weeks so a 40-employer university career fair could run entirely online."
>
  <article class="panel page">
    <a class="back mono" href="/creative/">← All projects</a>
    <h1 class="hl hl--page">
      Virtual Career Fair Platform
      <span>› A scheduling app built in six weeks so a 40-employer university career fair could run entirely online, and be trusted by both sides of every interview</span>
    </h1>

    <dl class="facts">
      {meta.map(([k, v]) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="mono">{k}</dt>
          <dd>{v}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <div class="case">
      <div>
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <p>
          Scheduling was running on a shared spreadsheet and a mailing list. Students didn't know which slots were
          real, recruiters double-booked, and organisers spent the fair on the phone reconciling both. Nobody could
          see the same picture at the same time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>
          Designed and built the whole thing in React: recruiters publish slots, students book against live
          availability, organisers watch the board fill. The student flow is three screens — browse, pick, confirm —
          and availability is the only state that ever changes on screen, so a stale slot can't be booked.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Constraints</h2>
        <p>
          Most students would open it once, on a phone, on university wifi, with no instructions. That ruled out
          onboarding, saved preferences, and anything that needed a second visit to make sense.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Outcome</h2>
        <p>
          Over 100 interviews scheduled in the first run with no manual reconciliation, and the faculty brought the
          platform back for the following year's fair.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="facts facts--big">
      {stats.map(([n, l]) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="mono">{l}</dt>
          <dd>{n}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn mono" href="/creative/">All projects</a>
      <a class="btn mono" href={site.links.behance} target="_blank" rel="noopener">More on Behance ↗</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
